  "title": "Pothus, 26 May 1940",
  "map": "pothus",
  "minutes": 45,
  "prepMinutes": 8,
  "briefing": "The ridge on the east bank was lost yesterday afternoon; the last men off it crossed the flooded side river on a rope of rifle slings. The west bank held: the Germans never got over at the bridge. In the night they built a pontoon bridge upstream and moved their weight to the west flank. The outpost on the hillside has been pushed back, and the last reserve, men of No. 2 Independent Company, is going up the slope to stop the Germans getting round behind. Evacuation from Bodø has been decided: the retreat begins at seven in the evening. Hold the west bank until then.",
  "alliedRole": "Defend the west bank: two sections of No. 4 Company at the bridge, No. 3 Company, the Norwegian mortars and machine gun, and No. 2 Independent Company on the hillside. Stockforce HQ can call the 25-pounders twice more.",
  "germanRole": "Attack from the west bank, having crossed on the pontoon bridge upstream in the night, while the squads on the ridge fire across. Take the hillside and get behind the bridge. The Zugtrupp can call the mountain guns and the Heinkels.",
